# L §4.6 step 1: "its governs span contains the period of x's time key when x is keyed by a period ... A span
# contains a period when it contains the period's first day, so 2025-04-06..2026-04-05 governs key 2025 of
# year … from 04-06."  An input keyed by the period read in an ask with no law: the key decides.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

index tys = year 2024..2026 from 04-06
input allowance[t in tys]: int

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2025-04-06..2026-04-05
  known 2025-01-01
  allowance[*] = 7

ask q1: allowance[2025], allowance[2024]
=== expect
q1: (7, ?"allowance at 2024: no value for 2024" (allowance[2024]))
  cut 2026-12-31
